"The journeyman who slept here, Ansel Pike, is posted to the western border and writes to no one."
"Nala cannot light the lamp or run the tap until she learns the activation glyph."
"The room sits almost straight above Hallick's locked drawer, one floor down."
"Tessa Voyle is the apprentice sent up at eight to fetch the new bench hand."
"Hallick expected her at the bench on her first morning; a no-show costs her some of his regard."
"Her first sleep under the Spire's coverage, the worn augera brushes her dreams, curious."
"She dreams of a vast still sea under a lightless sky, and of being looked at from inside it."
